course: dictionary
lesson: 15913
title: Unoccupied means empty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unoccupied means empty, with nobody using it or living in it. «The unoccupied house had a For Sale sign in the garden.» Nobody lives there, so unoccupied means empty. The clues around the word show you the meaning.
explain: Unoccupied can describe a seat, a room or a place with no one in it. «Every seat on the bus was occupied except one.» The word except tells you that one seat is unoccupied, so it is free to sit in.
explain: Unoccupied can also mean not busy, with nothing to do. «After lunch, the teacher sat in an unoccupied corner and read.» Ask: what word would fit here? Try empty in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Unoccupied is made of un- (not) and occupied (taken or in use). So unoccupied means not taken or not in use.
fact: «Unoccupied» means empty, with nobody using it or living in it.
fact: «Vacant» is a close synonym: an unoccupied seat is a vacant seat.
fact: In maths, unoccupied = total − occupied. If a car park has 40 spaces and 25 are taken, then 15 spaces are unoccupied.
exercise: «The unoccupied house had no lights on at night.» What does unoccupied mean here? | Full of guests for a party | *Empty, with nobody living in it | Loud and busy with music | Painted bright blue
exercise: «Every seat on the bus was occupied except one.» Which seat was unoccupied? | All the seats together | Mia's seat, where she is sitting | The seat at the front | *The one empty seat
exercise: Ella says unoccupied means busy. What does unoccupied really mean? | Very busy and full of people | *Not busy, with nothing to do | Dirty and messy | Noisy and loud
test: «Are there any unoccupied seats left?» In a cinema, what does unoccupied mean? | *Empty, with no one sitting there | Sold out and full | Broken and dirty | Reserved for famous people
test: A car park has 40 spaces and 25 cars. How many spaces are unoccupied? | *15 | 65 | 40 | 25
exam: Which word means nearly the same as unoccupied, as in «a vacant seat»? | Busy | Heavy | Occupied | *Vacant
